  "final_report": "[stop_reason: hop_cap_reached | hops used: 4/4]\n\nAnalyst summary:\n**Investigation\u202fsummary \u2013 disruption at Aneka Tambang\u202fTbk (AT)**  \n\n| Down\u2011stream / partner company (identified in the supply\u2011graph) | Tier | Evidence found | What could not be confirmed |\n|---|---|---|---|\n| **BHP Group Ltd.** | 1 (joint\u2011venture partner on Gag Island) | \u2022 BHP filing (2004\u202f&\u202f2005\u202fForm\u202f20\u2011F excerpts) states: \u201cWe hold a\u202f75\u202f% managing interest in the Gag Island project in Indonesia with Aneka Tambang holding the remaining\u202f25\u202f% interest.\u201d This directly links AT to BHP\u2019s nickel\u2011cobalt project and shows that any disruption at AT could affect BHP\u2019s supply of nickel/cobalt from Gag Island. | \u2013 |\n| **PT Perusahaan Listrik Negara (PLN)** \u2013 Indonesian state electricity utility | 1 (listed as a downstream customer) | No filing or corpus mention was returned for PLN in the limited searches performed. | No SEC\u2011filing excerpt or corpus hit that ties PLN to AT\u2019s output; the relationship remains unverified. |\n| **POSCO** (South Korea) \u2013 steel producer | 1 (listed as a downstream customer) | No specific filing or corpus reference linking POSCO to AT was retrieved. The large POSCO tables returned by the corpus search contain only internal balance\u2011sheet data and do not mention AT. | No direct evidence of a supply relationship; cannot confirm impact. |\n| **Glencore** (UK) \u2013 metals & mining, cobalt producer | 1 (listed as a downstream customer) | A `get_supplier_info` call for Glencore returned \u201cNo filings on record.\u201d | No filing or corpus mention that connects Glencore to AT\u2019s nickel/cobalt output. |\n| **SeAH Steel Corp.** (South Korea) \u2013 steel pipes & tubes | 1 | No filing or corpus hit found. | Unconfirmed. |\n| **Krakatau Steel\u202fPersero\u202fTbk** (Indonesia) \u2013 hot\u2011rolled/coiled steel | 1 | No filing or corpus hit found. | Unconfirmed. |\n| **Mitsui\u202f&\u202fCo.** (Japan) \u2013 metals trading | 1 | No filing or corpus hit found. | Unconfirmed. |\n| **Other Tier\u20112 companies** (e.g., Samsung\u202fSDI, LG\u202fEnergy\u202fSolution, Tesla, Umicore, etc.) | 2 | No filing or corpus hit found for any of these entities that specifically references AT. | All remain unverified. |\n\n### What the evidence tells us\n* **Confirmed link:** The only concrete, source\u2011level confirmation we located is the joint\u2011venture between AT and **BHP** on the Gag Island nickel\u2011cobalt project. BHP\u2019s 75\u202f% stake means that any production shortfall at AT could directly reduce the material supply feeding BHP\u2019s downstream processing and sales activities.\n* **Likely exposure (structural):** The supply\u2011graph shows many large steel, battery\u2011material and electric\u2011utility firms (POSCO, Glencore, PLN, SeAH, Krakatau Steel, Mitsui, Samsung\u202fSDI, LG\u202fEnergy\u202fSolution, Tesla, Umicore, etc.) that are *structurally* downstream of AT \u2013 i.e., they consume nickel, cobalt or other metal products that AT produces.  \n  However, **no SEC filing excerpts or corpus mentions** were retrieved that explicitly document a material supply relationship with AT for any of these firms within the limited tool\u2011call budget.\n* **Unconfirmed exposures:** For all companies listed above except BHP, we could not locate documentary proof (company\u2011self\u2011filings or third\u2011party filings) confirming that they source material from AT. Consequently, while the graph suggests a potential risk, the investigation cannot substantiate it with filed evidence.\n\n### Gaps & incomplete parts of the investigation\n* **No filing evidence** for PLN, POSCO, Glencore, SeAH, Krakatau Steel, Mitsui and the many Tier\u20112 firms.  \n* The supply\u2011graph contains **hundreds of additional companies** (e.g., Samsung\u202fElectronics, Hyundai Motor, ArcelorMittal, etc.) that are two tiers away; we did not have enough tool calls to verify each individually.\n* No information was found on the **specific nature or volume** of AT\u2019s shipments to these downstream entities, so the materiality of any disruption remains uncertain beyond the confirmed BHP joint\u2011venture.\n\n### Bottom line\n- **Confirmed at\u2011risk company:** **BHP Group Ltd.** \u2013 its Gag Island nickel\u2011cobalt project is a 75\u202f%/25\u202f% partnership with AT; AT\u2019s disruption could directly affect BHP\u2019s supply chain.\n- **Potentially at\u2011risk companies (structurally downstream):** PT PLN, POSCO, Glencore, SeAH Steel, Krakatau Steel, Mitsui, Samsung\u202fSDI, LG\u202fEnergy\u202fSolution, Tesla, Umicore and many others.  \n  *Evidence for these links was not found in the filings searched; their exposure remains **unverified**.*  \n\nFurther research would require additional filing pulls (e.g., targeted `get_supplier_info` calls for each major downstream firm) or broader corpus searches with company\u2011specific filters to confirm whether they actually source nickel, cobalt or other products from Aneka Tambang.\n\nCOVERAGE GAPS (98) -- reported explicitly, not omitted:\n  - perusahaan perseroan persero pt perusahaan listrik negara: no evidence gathered\n  - waskita karya persero tbk pt: no evidence gathered\n  - glencore: no evidence gathered\n  - seah: no evidence gathered\n  - krakatau steel persero tbk pt: no evidence gathered\n  - mitsui: no evidence gathered\n  - seah besteel: no evidence gathered\n  - gunung raja paksi tbk pt: no evidence gathered\n  - xiamen tungsten: no evidence gathered\n  - toagosei: no evidence gathered\n  - zhejiang juhua: no evidence gathered\n  - guangzhou tinci materials technology: no evidence gathered\n  - posco international: no evidence gathered\n  - schaeffler: no evidence gathered\n  - dongsung chemical: no evidence gathered\n  - gestamp automocion: no evidence gathered\n  - hd korea shipbuilding & 